                <pb facs="0846" n="756" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg756"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.6363/115: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-11-08T21:00:00+09:00">November 8, 1934—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 8—9:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>250. My 244, November 6, 7 p.m. The Netherlands Minister has informed me that
                    this morning he sent to his Government a long telegram explaining the oil
                    situation in Japan and stating that in his <pb facs="0847" n="757"
                        xml:id="pg757"/> opinion there is no hope of obtaining any amelioration of
                    the situation unless the foreign oil companies and the British, American and
                    Netherlands Governments present a united front to the Japanese.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
